{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_f0695830b5417b7e\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_f0695830b5417b7e/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Major error classification for incorrect year\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_7dd7657aac06c540713f3871\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether one wrong year in an otherwise correct answer counts as a major error on RP-8851.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In this thread, the team lead asks for the question and incorrect fact to assess whether the fact drives the final answer, explaining that the same wrong year can be minor background context or major in a chronology task. Verbatim quote: \\\"Share the question and the incorrect fact. We need to know whether that fact drives the final answer. The same wrong year can be minor in background context and major in a chronology task.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current project instructions classify a factual error as major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on, and as minor when it is nonessential background with no effect on that conclusion.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The available thread does not supply the original question or incorrect fact requested by the team lead, leaving the classification of RP-8851 pending those inputs.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868903.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether one wrong year in an otherwise correct answer counts as a major error on RP-8851.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The team lead has explained that the year’s importance depends on whether it drives the final answer, rather than being background context.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead requested the original question and incorrect fact; neither is supplied in the available thread, so the task-specific classification remains pending.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868903.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:no_action\", \"kind\": \"NO_ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why no further action is needed now: The team lead’s explanation matches current guidance, and the task-specific assessment awaits requested inputs rather than a new handling rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868903.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_7dd7657aac06c540713f3871\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_7dd7657aac06c540713f3871 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The QA tutor’s general question received a contextual answer from the team lead, but classification of the specific task awaits the requested question and incorrect fact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868903.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: This is a localized classification question with a contextual explanation already provided; the messages do not report conflicting judgments or broader workflow impact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868851.000023\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7dd7657aac06c540713f3871\", \"thread_id\": \"1790868851.000023\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:34:11.000023Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Would one wrong year in an otherwise correct answer count as a major error? (task ref RP-8851)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868903.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7dd7657aac06c540713f3871\", \"thread_id\": \"1790868851.000023\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:35:03.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Would correcting this error change the answer a user acts on? The evaluator needs the original question before deciding whether this fact is central.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790868946.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7dd7657aac06c540713f3871\", \"thread_id\": \"1790868851.000023\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:35:46.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Share the question and the incorrect fact. We need to know whether that fact drives the final answer. The same wrong year can be minor in background context and major in a chronology task.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors and citations\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors and citations\\n- A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\\n- A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n- A broken link is an access/verification failure, not proof that the underlying factual claim is false.\\n- Distinguish an existing source that does not support the claim from an invented reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual secondary requirement | A stylistic choice that violates no requirement |\\n| Citation support | Fabricated reference or materially unsupported attribution | A limited citation-detail error where the source and support remain identifiable | A valid source that supports the claim |\\n| Preference | Identify a meaningful benefit; grade underlying defects separately | Do not manufacture a defect to break a tie | No meaningful quality difference supports a tie |\\n\\nAn inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the error grade of the claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors\\n\\n### Q: What counts as a significant factual error?\\nAn error that changes the central conclusion or the answer the user would act on. A nonessential background detail with no effect on the recommendation is minor.\\n\\n### Q: The source link is dead. Should I penalize the factual claim?\\nRecord that the citation could not be verified. A failed URL alone does not prove the claim is false. Distinguish access failure from an unsupported attribution or fabricated reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction following\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction following\\n\\n### Q: The prompt required JSON, but one response is well-written prose. Which response wins?\\nThe required format is not optional: record its violation separately from factual accuracy. No universal tie-break rule is established for competing accuracy and instruction-following defects. If the actual pair and applicable guidance do not settle the preference, provide the prompt and both responses for TL confirmation.\\n\\n### Q: Can accuracy outweigh ignoring a requested output structure?\\nScore the dimensions separately and identify whether the requested structure was mandatory. Do not infer a general priority rule from one example or decide without the other response's evidence.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Calibration\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Calibration\\nFor comparable pairs receiving different judgments, retain both rationales and the relevant evidence. A scoped answer about one pair does not automatically become a new universal preference rule.\"}], \"open_review_flags\": [], \"governing_sources\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\"], \"declared_conflicts\": [], \"scenario_id\": \"topic:cluster_f0695830b5417b7e/topic_1\", \"stage\": \"grounding\", \"output_schema\": {\"$defs\": {\"ActionSufficiency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Whether the premises that passed justify the exact proposed action (wording, conditions and scope).\", \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"SUFFICIENT\", \"INSUFFICIENT\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"essential_statement_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"verdict\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"AlternativeSufficiency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"The same sufficiency judgment for one reviewed ToT alternative (statement_id alternative:<candidate>).\", \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"SUFFICIENT\", \"INSUFFICIENT\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"essential_statement_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"statement_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"verdict\", \"rationale\", \"statement_id\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"DeclaredConflictCheck\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"The judge's check of one conflict the draft declared (by its index in declared_conflicts).\", \"properties\": {\"conflict_index\": {\"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}, \"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"CONFIRMED\", \"SOURCES_AGREE\", \"UNDETERMINED\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"conflict_index\", \"verdict\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"SourceConsistency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"assessed_evidence_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"relations\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRelation\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"declared_conflict_checks\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DeclaredConflictCheck\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"type\": \"object\"}, \"SourceRelation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Governing sources that address the same point: AGREE or CONFLICT (with the scope of the disagreement).\", \"properties\": {\"evidence_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"relation\": {\"enum\": [\"AGREE\", \"CONFLICT\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"point\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"disagreement_scope\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"evidence_ids\", \"relation\", \"point\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"StatementVerdict\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"statement_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"SUPPORTED\", \"PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\", \"UNSUPPORTED\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"statement_id\", \"verdict\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"One verdict per statement presented (claims, summary, action, severity, reporters, resolution,\\nannouncement handling, source agreement and ToT alternatives), plus the sufficiency judgment for the action\\nand for each operational alternative sent. v5: source_consistency (required).\", \"properties\": {\"contract_version\": {\"default\": \"agent3-grounding-judgment-v5\", \"enum\": [\"agent3-grounding-judgment-v5\", \"agent3-grounding-judgment-v4\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"verdicts\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/StatementVerdict\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"action_sufficiency\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ActionSufficiency\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"alternative_sufficiency\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AlternativeSufficiency\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"source_consistency\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceConsistency\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"verdicts\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object for GroundingJudgment matching output_schema. No prose outside the JSON.\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: One GroundingJudgment JSON object.\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nProvide your complete response:"}],"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","max_completion_tokens":16384,"reasoning_effort":"medium","response_format":{"type":"json_object"},"service_tier":"default"}